title: A staged rename whose file was changed afterwards, and a file deleted on disk: the panel and the diff show them (the renamed file against its old name), the deleted file is staged and unstaged, discarded (it comes back); the renamed file with all of it staged has nothing to discard, and changed again it goes back to what is staged, still renamed
folders: git-rename-staged
expect-file: git-rename-staged/src/removed.rs :: ^pub fn removed\(\) \{\}\n$
expect-file: git-rename-staged/src/new_name.rs :: ^pub fn kept\(\) -> u32 \{\n    100\n\}\n\npub fn also\(\) -> u32 \{\n    2\n\}\n$
absent-file: git-rename-staged/src/old_name.rs
expect-log: what changed is shown inside 1 files
forbid-log: script: ignoring
forbid-log: nothing offers

wait 3000
left changes
wait 500
mark 1-panel
wait 500
diff on
wait 1500
goto src/new_name.rs
wait 1200
mark 2-diff-renamed
wait 500
diff off
wait 800
part stage src/new_name.rs 2
wait 1500
mark 3-part-staged
wait 500
git stage src/removed.rs
wait 1200
mark 4-deletion-staged
wait 500
git unstage src/removed.rs
wait 1200
git discard src/removed.rs
wait 600
answer Discard
wait 1500
mark 5-deleted-file-back
wait 500
git discard src/new_name.rs
wait 600
mark 6-nothing-to-discard
wait 500
touch src/new_name.rs // changed after staging
wait 2500
git discard src/new_name.rs
wait 600
mark 7-asked
wait 500
answer Discard
wait 1500
mark 8-renamed-discarded
wait 500
quit
